{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And Jeshurun grew fat.</b> Israel. And it is possible that it is from the root ישר, and the meaning is: this one grew fat who was upright. And some say that it is from the root אשורנו. And the first is the correct one in my eyes, and the proof is that it is singular in form." "<b>And he kicked.</b> Like למה תבעטו, according to the meaning of the verse." "<b>You grew fat.</b> And they did not think to say to himself." "<b>You grew thick.</b> Like קטני עבה." "<b>You were covered.</b> Some say it is like כסה פניו בחלבו, for it is found in the light [binyan kal] construction. And others said it is like תעיתי כשה אובד, and this [some say not] is found in one of the doubled stems. And the correct one in my eyes is that this word has no cognate, and its meaning is like 'you kicked'." "<b>And he forsook.</b> The commandments of his Elohim." "<b>And he treated with contempt.</b> In thought and in speech. And the correct interpretation is that he profaned the name of the one who did not save him — he turned away; therefore it is written 'the Rock of his salvation.' Also this verse is according to the reading of the Rock, whose deed is perfect."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "Resolved י״‎א as 'some say' based on parallel usage throughout the commentary.", 4 "The parenthetical (ס״‎א לא) indicates a variant reading in some witnesses; translated literally as '[some say not]'. The phrase הפעלים is rendered 'doubled stems' following Ibn Ezra's grammatical usage."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:01.172078775Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}